  {
   "n": 16,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>Consider the following statements regarding relations:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Every asymmetric relation is irreflexive.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Every asymmetric relation is antisymmetric.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : There are some relations which are neither reflexive nor irreflexive.<br />\nWhich of the above statements are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> but not <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\tS2 only</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "None of these"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a)<br />\nFor <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>: If a relation is asymmetric, then it has to be both irreflexive and antisymmetric.<br />\nTherefore <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> are correct.<br />\nFor <em>S</em><sub>3</sub>: It is true that there are some relations which are neither irreflexive (contain at least one self loop) nor reflexive (don&rsquo;t contain all self loops).<br />\nSo all the statements are correct.</p>"
  },
